			"date": "2024-07-05T16:26:44.340Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@colepeters\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>colepeters</span></a></span> I’m not sure we’re quite connecting on the point</p><p>If a serif label on a navigation menu suddenly changed to sans-serif, the assumptions about the dimensions at which it was coded (especially for responsive design breakpoints or text overflow) would change. Of course this would only impact sites that did not have font-family application styles but that’s certainly more than zero and would still count as breaking the web</p>",
